.SS "int get_clicked_button (GtkWidget * button, \fBGameUI\fP * ui)"

.PP
Obtains the button number that was clicked\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
-1 in case the elements do not match, otherwise the button number {1, 2, 3}
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbutton\fP a pointer to a GtkWidget, which is supposed to be a button\&. 
.br
\fIui\fP the \fBGameUI\fP, it holds a pointer too each action buttons in the program 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void on_action_clicked (GtkWidget * button, gpointer data)"

.PP
Handles the action when clicked\&. Handles the action button click, apply the changes to the planet and starts a new game turn\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbutton\fP a GtkWidget pointer that should represent a button\&. 
.br
\fIdata\fP the data provided by the callback, it should be of type \fBGameUI\fP * 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void on_window_destroy (GtkWidget * widget, gpointer data)"

.PP
Callback to the signal of window destroy\&. Properly disposes of elements in memory\&. Destroys the planet and the \fBGameUI\fP by freeing the memory, then calls gtk_main_quit() to exit the program\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwidget\fP a GtkWidget (probably the main window) 
.br
\fIdata\fP the data provided by the callback, it should be of type \fBGameUI\fP * 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void runGUIGame (int argc, char * argv[])"

.PP
Runs the full game, turn by turn, until win condition or game over is reached\&. This function will initialize everything to a playable state, before launching the game loop, once the loop stops it will handle memory deallocation as well\&.

.PP
